    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A couple months ago, I emailed a recipe for </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/oatmeal-cookie-dough-bites/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Oatmeal Cookie Dough Bites</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and they were such a hit that I wanted to share another healthy sweet treat. These <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/brownie-sandwich-cookies/\">brownie cookies</a> have a date-sweetened creamy filling and are a great way to get a serving of beans</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">—yes! beans!—</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">while satisfying a sweet tooth. Check out the recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/brownie-sandwich-cookies/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and watch a video on how they’re made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CXeXLenp6tw/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Help Us Spread the Health</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-85373\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-960x960.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/sth-square.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>There’s still time to help us send 12,500 free copies of our </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/healthkit\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evidence-Based Eating Guide</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to health care practitioners in all 50 states. Just $20 allows us to print and ship 16 copies of the guide to a doctor’s office, hospital, or health clinic. With increased publishing and shipping costs, we’d be even more grateful for your help in getting them directly into the hands of the very people whose lives can be changed with our practical guide to healthy eating.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Please consider </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.neoncrm.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=69&amp;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">making a donation</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to help us spread the health! </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Autism</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/autism/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-85363\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-960x960.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/autism.png 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>April is World Autism Month. Many families with a child on the autism spectrum pursue dietary and nutritional approaches as components of treatment. There are some dietary interventions that appear to be successful in helping to manage the troublesome symptoms of autism. One is sulforaphane, which is formed almost exclusively in cruciferous vegetables. Check out the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/autism/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a summary and a list of all of my autism videos, including </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/alternative-treatments-for-autism/\"><b>Alternative Treatments for Autism</b></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">and</span> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-foods-for-autism/\"><b>Best Foods for Autism</b></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Flashback Fridays Get a Refresh</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-85381\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/ff-logo.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"142\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/ff-logo.jpg 565w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/04/ff-logo-540x382.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/>Flashback Fridays are becoming Friday Favorites. I love resharing oldie-but-goodie videos for people who may have missed them the first time around, and those videos are getting a new look starting in May. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-60211\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"455\" height=\"147\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 455px) 100vw, 455px\"/></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-dont-people-eat-healthier/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-84952\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-960x540.jpeg\" alt=\"assorted fruit and nuts\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/why-dont-people-eat-healthier.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-dont-people-eat-healthier/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Don’t People Eat Healthier?</span></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The so-called optimism bias may get in the way of a healthy lifestyle.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-boost-fgf21-with-diet-for-longevity/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-72404\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"wooden bowls containing legumes and grains\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/57-7-How-to-Boost-FGF21-with-Diet-For-Longevity.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-boost-fgf21-with-diet-for-longevity/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Boost FGF21 with Diet for Longevity</span></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fasting and exercise can boost the longevity hormone FGF21, but what can we eat—or avoid eating—to get similar effects?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-keep-your-microbiome-healthy-with-prebiotic-foods/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-71488\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"a pile of fresh foods on a grey counter\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/01/57-5-How-to-Keep-Your-Microbiome-Healthy-With-Prebiotic-Foods.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-keep-your-microbiome-healthy-with-prebiotic-foods/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Keep Your Microbiome Healthy with Prebiotic Foods</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We co-evolved a symbiosis with our good gut bacteria, but we are not holding up our end of the bargain.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
